package.json:11:    "./*": "./app/*"
README.md:36:1. **Ember loads the screen.** The account route receives the ID from the URL and uses an injected API service to fetch the summary. The service loads Rails JSON into Ember Data records for users, accounts, and transactions. The account screen reads its balance and history from the account record. The form action reads `FormData` as strings. Tracked fields drive its saving, success, and error messages. [Route](app/routes/accounts/show.js) · [API service](app/services/accounts-api.js) · [Form](app/components/transaction-form.gjs)
README.md:37:2. **Rails checks access.** A Pundit scope limits the SQL query to the current user’s accounts. A policy answers whether that user can perform an action on a particular record. A lookup outside the scope returns `404`, which also covers an ID that does not exist. [Account policy](backend/app/policies/account_policy.rb) · [Transaction policy](backend/app/policies/transaction_policy.rb)
README.md:38:3. **PostgreSQL serializes writes to the account.** `with_lock` reloads the account and holds a row lock for the database transaction. The entry and balance update commit together. If a debit would overdraw the account, the balance validation raises and both writes roll back. Other processes using the same row must wait for the lock. A Ruby `Mutex` coordinates threads sharing that mutex in one process. [Write service](backend/app/services/post_transaction.rb)
README.md:39:4. **Money stays exact.** PostgreSQL `decimal(19, 2)` allows 17 whole digits and two decimal places. Rails parses amount strings into `BigDecimal` and returns balances, totals, and amounts as strings. Ember adds display separators as text. After a save, the API service updates the existing account record and its transaction history from the server response. [Decimal helper](backend/app/models/usd_amount.rb) · [Summary service](backend/app/services/account_summary.rb) · [Ember display helper](app/helpers/usd.js)
README.md:54:The SCSS uses simple typography, grouped cards, and direct form labels inspired by Upstart’s public product pages. Tokens and layout rules live in one place. [Upstart personal loans](https://www.upstart.com/personal-loans) · [SCSS](app/styles/accounts-dashboard.scss)
